# Files remain locally as caches; the warehouse is the tracked store.
cache_seed/ltm/US.parquet
cache_seed/ltm/JP.parquet
cache_seed/ltm/KR.parquet
cache_seed/ltm/CN.parquet
cache_seed/ltm/IN.parquet
*.bak
warehouse/etl_registry.sqlite

# ── price panels: migrated out of git 2026-08-17 ──────────────────────────────
# The note above ("the warehouse is the tracked store") is no longer true for
# these two trees. 909 MB of year-partitioned parquet now lives in the cloud
# store and is reached through ~/scripts/market_paths.py, which materialises it
# into ~/.cache/market-warehouse on demand:
#
#     dropbox:market-data-archive/current/gmd_warehouse/ohlcv       (66 files)
#     dropbox:market-data-archive/current/gmd_warehouse/ohlcv_adj   (14 files)
#
# 🔴 WHY THEY ARE IGNORED AND NOT MERELY DELETED. On 2026-08-14 these files were
# removed from the working tree WITHOUT being untracked. Git therefore kept
# insisting 94 files were missing, any `git checkout` resurrected them, and the
# two consumers still pointing at the old path failed three days later with "no
# warehouse partitions" (E-033). Untracking is the half that was skipped; doing
# only the delete is what caused the incident.
#
# Everything else under warehouse/ (bhavcopy/, cgd/, audit/, energy/,
# warehouse.duckdb, regimes.parquet, the adjustment_factors tables) was NOT part
# of that migration and stays tracked here.
warehouse/ohlcv/
warehouse/ohlcv_adj/
